WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.602
A content part is a group of fields that you define once and

00:00:04.602 --> 00:00:06.239
attach to content types.

00:00:06.239 --> 00:00:10.223
In this video, you create a Postal Address part and attach it twice

00:00:10.223 --> 00:00:13.770
to a Customer type, once for billing and once for shipping.

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:20.357
A content type is made of parts.

00:00:20.357 --> 00:00:22.343
A part adds something to a type:

00:00:22.343 --> 00:00:26.003
the Title part adds a title, and a part that you create yourself

00:00:26.003 --> 00:00:27.990
adds the fields that you choose.

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:32.669
You define a part once, and any content type can attach it, as

00:00:32.669 --> 00:00:34.807
long as the part is Attachable.

00:00:34.807 --> 00:00:39.141
A part marked Reusable can also be attached several times to the same

00:00:39.141 --> 00:00:41.510
type, each time under its own name.

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:44.926
A postal address is a typical example:

00:00:44.926 --> 00:00:47.410
a street, a city and a postal code.

00:00:47.410 --> 00:00:51.529
A customer needs one address for billing and one for shipping.

00:00:51.529 --> 00:00:55.770
Both can come from the same part, and each keeps its own values.

00:01:00.036 --> 00:01:04.278
In the admin menu, open Design, Content Definition, Content Parts.

00:01:04.278 --> 00:01:07.518
This page lists the parts that you can configure.

00:01:07.518 --> 00:01:09.226
Select Create new part.

00:01:11.159 --> 00:01:16.070
A part starts with a name, which cannot contain spaces or special characters.

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:20.449
We type PostalAddress, with the two words joined, and select Create.

00:01:20.903 --> 00:01:24.807
A message confirms that the content part has been created, and the editor

00:01:24.807 --> 00:01:25.993
of the part opens.

00:01:30.196 --> 00:01:33.355
The Technical Name is fixed once the part exists.

00:01:33.355 --> 00:01:37.491
The Display Name is what screens show, so we enter Postal Address.

00:01:37.491 --> 00:01:41.856
The Description appears next to the part when you attach it to a type.

00:01:42.316 --> 00:01:45.595
Attachable lets you attach the part to content types.

00:01:45.595 --> 00:01:49.706
A part that you create starts out attachable, so the box is checked.

00:01:50.158 --> 00:01:54.605
Reusable lets you attach the part more than once to the same type.

00:01:54.605 --> 00:01:57.138
We check Reusable, and select Save.

00:01:57.594 --> 00:02:01.438
A message confirms that the settings of the part are saved, and the

00:02:01.438 --> 00:02:03.544
page title shows the display name.

00:02:07.807 --> 00:02:09.525
The part has no fields.

00:02:09.525 --> 00:02:14.267
The Fields section lists them, and Add Field opens the form to create one.

00:02:14.756 --> 00:02:19.032
We enter Street as the Display Name, and the Technical Name follows.

00:02:19.032 --> 00:02:22.096
We choose the Text Field type, and select Save.

00:02:23.838 --> 00:02:27.994
The page returns to the part, with Street listed next to its type.

00:02:27.994 --> 00:02:30.938
We add City in the same way, as a Text Field.

00:02:34.159 --> 00:02:36.097
Last, we add Postal Code.

00:02:36.097 --> 00:02:41.599
The part holds three fields, and every type that attaches the part gets all three.

00:02:45.811 --> 00:02:48.177
Next, we attach the part to a type.

00:02:48.177 --> 00:02:52.792
On the Content Types page, Customer is a content type that already exists,

00:02:52.792 --> 00:02:54.177
with a Title part.

00:02:54.177 --> 00:02:56.081
We select Edit on Customer.

00:02:56.539 --> 00:02:59.562
The Parts section lists what the type is made of.

00:02:59.562 --> 00:03:03.026
Add Parts attaches an attachable part under its own name.

00:03:03.026 --> 00:03:07.149
Add Named Part attaches a reusable part under a name that you choose.

00:03:07.602 --> 00:03:09.706
Let's select Add Named Part.

00:03:09.706 --> 00:03:15.832
The page lists the parts that are both attachable and reusable, and we choose Postal Address.

00:03:16.296 --> 00:03:21.015
We enter Billing Address as the Display Name, and the Technical Name follows.

00:03:21.015 --> 00:03:23.516
We add a description, and select Save.

00:03:23.976 --> 00:03:27.269
Billing Address is listed among the parts of the type.

00:03:27.269 --> 00:03:31.550
We add the Postal Address part once more, this time as Shipping Address,

00:03:31.550 --> 00:03:33.526
with a description of its own.

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:37.495
The type has two named parts that share one definition.

00:03:37.495 --> 00:03:41.470
A field added to the Postal Address part later appears in both.

00:03:45.679 --> 00:03:50.699
On the Content Types page, Create New Customer opens the editor for a customer.

00:03:51.156 --> 00:03:57.124
Besides the Title, the editor has a group named Billing Address and another named Shipping Address.

00:03:57.124 --> 00:04:02.126
Each group shows its description, and the three fields of the Postal Address part.

00:04:02.587 --> 00:04:07.767
We enter a title, then the street, city and postal code of the billing address.

00:04:08.218 --> 00:04:10.711
The shipping address gets different values.

00:04:10.711 --> 00:04:13.559
Each name is a part of its own on the type, so the

00:04:13.559 --> 00:04:15.898
two groups keep their values separately.

00:04:16.351 --> 00:04:17.620
We select Publish.

00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:22.113
A message confirms that the customer has been published, and both addresses are

00:04:22.113 --> 00:04:23.911
saved with the content item.

00:04:25.911 --> 00:04:29.973
A content part groups fields that you define once, and Add Named Part

00:04:29.973 --> 00:04:33.602
attaches a reusable part to a type as many times as you need.

00:04:33.602 --> 00:04:35.011
Thanks for watching.

